            "content": "<!-- qualor:reply 4b18e4d9-7299-48a2-8e43-fa6e00007943 -->\n**AI review** · reply\n\nS1186 flags a function whose body is empty. An empty function is either unfinished or a silent no-op, and a reader cannot tell which. Here ` emptyHandler ` in ` probe/item-21-20261125104346.js ` (line 2) has a body with no statements, so callers get nothing and the intent is unclear. The rule applies to any function, not only handlers.\n\nTo fix it, pick the option that matches the intent. If the function should do something, implement it. If it is meant to do nothing on purpose, put a comment inside the braces saying why, such as ` // intentionally a no-op: ... `, which the rule accepts. If nothing calls it, delete it. If it is a placeholder, make it throw ` new Error('not implemented') ` so the gap is visible at runtime.",
