            "content": "<!-- qualor:summary d95a7a50-9013-4fa0-863c-fa6e00007afc -->\n### ❌ Qualor: quality gate failed\n\n**Qualor way** · analysis ` 0df46580001f ` · **1 new issue** in this pull request\n\n| | Condition | Value | Required |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ❌ | New issues | 1 | ≤ 0 |\n| ➖ | Coverage on new code | — | skipped: fewer than 20 new lines |\n| ➖ | Duplication on new code | — | skipped: fewer than 20 new lines |\n\n**By severity:** 🔴 1 high\n\n#### Most severe new issues\n\n1. 🔴 **High** · maintainability · [` sonarjs:S1186 `](https://sonarcloud.io/organizations/sonarsource/rules?open=javascript%3AS1186&rule_key=javascript%3AS1186) · [` probe/item-21-20261125104346.js:2 `](https://ado.example.invalid/projects/d95a7a50-9013-4fa0-863c-fa6e00007afc/issues/cd0c7fe9-fd86-4e03-8710-fa6e00002bdd)\\\n   Unexpected empty function ` 'emptyHandler' `.\n\n1 new issue is commented inline. · **[Open in Qualor →](https://ado.example.invalid/projects/d95a7a50-9013-4fa0-863c-fa6e00007afc/branches/1632955e-dfab-4fb8-8d01-fa6e0000f04a)**\n\n#### AI review\n\nTwo findings in the probe file: an inverted authorisation predicate (critical) with no test covering it, and a minor mismatch between the pipeline's header comment and its mutable image tag.\n\n**Findings:** 1 high · 1 medium · 1 low\n\n- ` probe/item-21-20261125104346.js ` adds an empty exported function emptyHandler (flagged by the analyzer) and the canDeleteAccount predicate.\n- canDeleteAccount returns ` !user.isAdmin `, which contradicts its doc comment saying only administrators may delete accounts.\n- No test in the repository references canDeleteAccount.\n- ` .azure-pipelines/qualor-docker.yml ` adds a pipeline that checks out the pull request head and runs the Qualor scanner in Docker.\n- The header comment claims the image tag is fixed, but the image is pinned only by the mutable tag azure-dev.\n\nReviewed commit: ` 0df46580001f `\n\n<details><summary>Prompt for an AI agent</summary>\n\n```text\nFix the problems below, which an AI review found in this pull request.\nThe review can be wrong: read the code first and skip a finding that does not hold.\nKeep each change small and run the tests afterwards.\n\n1. probe/item-21-20261125104346.js:6 canDeleteAccount is inverted: non-admins pass and administrators are refused\n   The doc comment says only administrators may delete accounts, but `!user.isAdmin` returns true for every non-admin and false for admins. Any caller that uses this predicate to authorise account deletion lets ordinary users delete accounts and blocks administrators. Change the expression to `user.isAdmin === true`, or a stricter role check, and add tests for an admin and a non-admin user. Callers are not in the diff, so the impact depends on their use of the predicate.\n2. probe/item-21-20261125104346.js:5 New account-deletion guard canDeleteAccount has no test\n   A grep of the repository finds `canDeleteAccount` only at its definition, so no test covers the guard that decides account deletion. A test asserting that an admin may delete and a non-admin may not would fail on the current code, which inverts the documented rule. Add that test with the fix to the predicate.\n3. .azure-pipelines/qualor-docker.yml:14 Header promises a fixed image tag, but qualor/scanner:azure-dev is a mutable tag\n   The header says \"The image tag is fixed: nothing floats\", yet `QUALOR_SCANNER_IMAGE` is `qualor/scanner:azure-dev`. A tag can be re-pushed to a different image, so the scan can run different code without any change to this file. Pin the image by digest, or reword the comment to say the tag is named but not immutable.\n```\n\n</details>",
