            "content": "<!-- qualor:issue 88af6fea-e8fb-4a54-805e-fa6e0000e635 -->\n**AI review** · High · Logic · likely · ` ai:logic `\n\n**canDeleteAccount is inverted: non-admins pass and administrators are refused**\n\nThe doc comment says only administrators may delete accounts, but ` !user.isAdmin ` returns true for every non-admin and false for admins. Any caller that uses this predicate to authorise account deletion lets ordinary users delete accounts and blocks administrators. Change the expression to ` user.isAdmin === true `, or a stricter role check, and add tests for an admin and a non-admin user. Callers are not in the diff, so the impact depends on their use of the predicate.\n\nAssumes: The predicate is used, or will be used, as an authorisation gate for account deletion; the callers are not in the snapshot.\n\n```suggestion\nexport const canDeleteAccount = (user) => user.isAdmin === true;\n```\n\n[View in Qualor](https://ado.example.invalid/projects/d95a7a50-9013-4fa0-863c-fa6e00007afc/issues/88af6fea-e8fb-4a54-805e-fa6e0000e635)",
